{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '148,228p' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt; sed -n '250,361p' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt; cat src/jolt/yin/repl/host.jolt; sed -n '634,665p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; sed -n '579,680p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '210,490p' src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '148,228p' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt; sed -n '250,361p' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt; cat src/jolt/yin/repl/host.jolt; sed -n '634,665p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; sed -n '579,680p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '210,490p' src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj\"","aggregated_output":"(defn host-pump\n  \"The instance as the driver's `:pump` value (A2): the pump's interest and\n   deadline (now while this edge owes a report), and `pump!`.\"\n  [inst]\n  (let [p (::pump inst)]\n    {:interest #(pump/interest p)\n     :deadline #(if (seq (:owed @(st inst))) (poller/clock-ms) (pump/next-deadline p))\n     :pump! (fn [ready]\n              (let [before? (deliver-owed! inst)\n                    r (pump/pump! p ready)\n                    after? (deliver-owed! inst)]\n                {:progressed? (boolean (or before? (:progressed? r) after?))}))}))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Frames\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- protocol\n  \"The pump's protocol map for `role` (:server or :client), whose parser\n   bounds a message at `max` bytes (nil is unbounded). Client frames are\n   masked with a fresh key each.\"\n  [role max]\n  (cond-> {:parser (rfc6455/parser {:role role, :max-message-bytes max})\n           :parse-frame rfc6455/parse-frame\n           :encode-frame rfc6455/encode-frame\n           :close-payload rfc6455/close-payload}\n    (= :client role) (assoc :mask-key crypto/mask-key)))\n\n\n(defn- data-frame\n  \"The wire bytes of one message: a string as a text frame, host bytes as a\n   binary frame; masked for the client role.\"\n  [role payload]\n  (rfc6455/encode-frame\n    (cond-> (if (string? payload)\n              {:opcode :text, :payload (text/utf8-encode payload)}\n              {:opcode :binary, :payload payload})\n      (= :client role) (assoc :mask-key (crypto/mask-key)))))\n\n\n(defn- deliver-message!\n  [cb ev]\n  (when cb\n    (let [payload (:payload ev)]\n      (if (= :text (:opcode ev))\n        ((:message! cb) (text/utf8-decode payload 0 (alength payload)))\n        ((:binary! cb) payload)))))\n\n\n(defn- report-closed!\n  \"The one terminal of an upgraded connection, from the pump's owed\n   `:on-closed`.\"\n  [cb {:keys [code reason cause]}]\n  (when cb\n    (when (and (= :fail cause) (= 1009 code))\n      ((:too-large! cb)))\n    ((:closed! cb) code reason)))\n\n\n(defn- seam\n  \"The raw-socket seam over connection record `c`, whose role frames\n   outbound messages.\"\n  [p c role]\n  {:send! (fn [payload]\n            (let [{:keys [phase h]} @c]\n              (if (= :open phase)\n                (pump/send! p h (data-frame role payload))\n                pump/closed-outcome)))\n   :close! (fn [code reason]\n             (let [{:keys [phase h]} @c]\n               (when (= :open phase) (pump/close! p h code reason)))\n             nil)\n   :queued-bytes #(if-let [h (:h @c)] (pump/queued-bytes h) 0)})\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Dialer\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- random-key\n(defn- client-request!\n  \"Send the upgrade request on dialed connection `c` once it is connected.\n   A failed write is reported by the pump through `:on-error`.\"\n  [inst c]\n  (let [{:keys [h request]} @c]\n    (swap! c assoc :phase :upgrading)\n    (pump/send! (::pump inst) h (text/utf8-encode request))\n    nil))\n\n\n(defn- client-head!\n  \"Response head bytes on dialed connection `c`.\"\n  [inst c chunk]\n  (when (= :upgrading (:phase @c))\n    (let [{:keys [head-parser key offered h cb]} @c\n          [hp result] (upgrade/head-feed head-parser chunk)]\n      (swap! c assoc :head-parser hp)\n      (cond\n        (nil? result) nil\n        (:refused result) (client-failed! inst c 1006 connect-failed)\n        :else\n        (let [verdict (upgrade/check-response (upgrade/parse-response (:head result))\n                                              {:key key, :offered offered, :sha1 crypto/sha1})]\n          (if (not= :ok (:outcome verdict))\n            (client-failed! inst c 1006 connect-failed)\n            (do (pump/upgraded! (::pump inst) h (protocol :client (:ws/max-frame-bytes cb))\n                                (:rest result))\n                (swap! c assoc :phase :open)\n                ((:opened! cb)))))))))\n\n\n(defn- secure?\n  [descriptor]\n  (= \"wss\" (:ws/scheme descriptor)))\n\n\n(defn connect!\n  \"Start dialing `descriptor` (`:ws/host` a literal or localhost, `:ws/port`,\n   `:ws/path`) with composition callbacks `cb` (the `dao.stream.ws/adapter`\n   shape; `:ws/codec` names the one subprotocol offered, none without it).\n   Never waits. Answers the seam, or nil for an address this host does not\n   dial (a host name, the wss scheme) or a closed instance. The upgrade\n   request is built, and an invalid field refused (thrown), before any\n   socket exists. A connect that fails reports its one `:closed!` on a later\n   turn.\"\n  [inst descriptor cb]\n  (let [p (::pump inst)\n        addr (tcp/parse-address (:ws/host descriptor) (:ws/port descriptor))]\n    (when (and (live? inst) (not (secure? descriptor)) (not (:error addr)))\n      (let [offered (if-let [c (:ws/codec cb)] [(codec/codec-name c)] [])\n            key (random-key)\n            {:keys [head]} (upgrade/client-request {:host (:ws/host descriptor)\n                                                    :port (:ws/port descriptor)\n                                                    :path (:ws/path descriptor)\n                                                    :key key\n                                                    :subprotocols offered})\n            c (atom {:phase :connecting, :role :client, :cb cb, :offered offered\n                     :key key, :request head, :head-parser (upgrade/head-parser)})\n            r (tcp/connect! addr)]\n        (if (:error r)\n          (do (swap! c assoc :phase :closed)\n              (owe! inst #((:closed! cb) 1006 connect-failed)))\n          (let [opts (::opts inst)\n                fail #(client-failed! inst c 1006 connect-failed)\n                h (pump/connection!\n                    p (:fd r)\n                    (cond-> {:connecting? (= :connecting (:state r))\n                             :upgrading? true\n                             :on-connected (gated inst #(client-request! inst c))\n                             :on-data (gated inst #(client-head! inst c %))\n                             :on-eof (gated inst fail)\n                             :on-error (gated inst (fn [_] (fail)))\n                             :on-upgrade-expired (gated inst fail)\n                             :on-message (gated inst #(deliver-message! cb %))\n                             :on-closed (gated inst (fn [t]\n                                                      (swap! c assoc :phase :closed)\n                                                      (forget! inst c)\n                                                      (report-closed! cb t)))}\n                      (:upgrade-timeout-ms opts) (assoc :upgrade-timeout-ms (:upgrade-timeout-ms opts))\n                      (:close-deadline-ms opts) (assoc :close-deadline-ms (:close-deadline-ms opts))))]\n            (swap! c assoc :h h)\n            (swap! (st inst) update :conns conj c)\n            (when (= :connected (:state r))\n              (client-request! inst c))))\n        (assoc (seam p c :client)\n               :close! (fn [code reason]\n                         (let [{:keys [phase h]} @c]\n                           (case phase\n                             :open (pump/close! p h code reason)\n                             :closed nil\n                             ;; before the upgrade: no frame exists to close with\n                             (do (swap! c assoc :phase :closed)\n                                 (when h (pump/discard! p h))\n                                 (forget! inst c)\n                                 (owe! inst #((:closed! cb) code reason)))))\n                         nil))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Listener\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private failure-text\n  {:yin.repl.endpoint/subprotocol-required \"the WebSocket upgrade offered no supported subprotocol\"\n   :yin.repl.endpoint/websocket-required \"the request was not a WebSocket upgrade\"\n   :yin.repl.endpoint/bad-request \"the WebSocket upgrade request was invalid\"\n   :yin.repl.endpoint/head-too-large \"the WebSocket upgrade head exceeded 8 KiB\"\n   :yin.repl.endpoint/upgrade-expired \"the WebSocket upgrade did not complete in time\"\n   :yin.repl.endpoint/upgrade-threw \"the host failed while accepting an upgrade\"\n   :yin.repl.endpoint/socket-error \"the socket failed before the upgrade completed\"})\n\n\n(ns yin.repl.host\n  \"The jolt composition of the Yin REPL host WebSocket seam (J6e).\n\n   This jolt namespace shadows the `.cljc` one, so it carries only\n   `websocket`; the portable contract is `yin.repl.host.common`. It\n   composes the native RFC 6455 edge (`dao.stream.ws.jolt`) for the REPL:\n   upgrades reach `dao.stream.ws/accept-connection!` through the endpoint's\n   `accept!`, and each accepted connection reports through the\n   `dao.stream.ws/adapter` of its handle.\n\n   Unlike the JVM, Node and Dart packages, jolt's sockets move only when\n   their owner pumps them, so the adapter also carries `:pump` (the\n   driver's `{:interest :deadline :pump!}`, A2) and `:close-host!` (forced\n   cleanup once the owner loop has ended, A6). One instance per call: two\n   adapters never share a descriptor.\"\n  (:require [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n            [dao.stream.ws.jolt :as wsj]))\n\n\n(defn websocket\n  \"Return a fresh jolt host adapter: `{:connect! :bind! :unbind! :pump\n   :close-host! :debug-state}` over one new instance. `opts` (tests only):\n   `:upgrade-timeout-ms`, `:close-deadline-ms`.\"\n  ([] (websocket nil))\n  ([opts]\n   (let [inst (wsj/create opts)]\n     {:connect! (fn [descriptor adapter] (wsj/connect! inst descriptor adapter))\n      :bind! (fn [options]\n               (wsj/bind! inst (assoc options :ws.jolt/adapter-of\n                                      #(some-> (:ws/handle %) ws/adapter))))\n      :unbind! (fn [listener deposit!] (wsj/unbind! inst listener deposit!))\n      :pump (wsj/host-pump inst)\n      :close-host! #(wsj/close-host! inst)\n      :debug-state #(wsj/debug-state inst)})))\n(defn boot\n  \"Create the composition: one shell, one input medium, one cursor held only by\n   the step owner, and the host WebSocket adapter `(connect ...)` attaches\n   through.  The parsed `:index-store-spec` reaches the shell's store\n   selection, which resolves and opens it once at construction.  A custody\n   composition (:custody, yin.vm.ucf.compose) rides the shell as data; the\n   step owner below is the only thing that steps it.\n\n   `:admission` is the session's admission policy (yin.vm.linker.dht.md\n   7.5; `--dht-trust` sets its `:trusted`), by default `{}`: the key's\n   own principal only.  It is apart from `:principals`: a declared\n   publisher is not a trusted one.\"\n  ([] (boot {}))\n  ([opts] (driver/create-state\n            {:host (or (:adapter opts) (host/websocket))\n             :repl (repl.frontends/create-state\n                     (cond-> {:index-store-spec (:index-store-spec opts)\n                              :dht-key (:dht-key opts)\n                              :principals (:principals opts)\n                              :admission (:admission opts {})\n                              :ws-host (:ws-host opts)\n                              :write-heads! (:write-heads! opts)\n                              :custody (:custody opts)}\n                       (:vm-type opts) (assoc :vm-type (:vm-type opts))))})))\n\n\n(def bind-all-host\n  \"`--port` listens on every interface: loopback and the machine's own IP.\"\n  \"0.0.0.0\")\n\n\n(defn pick-ip\n(defn repl-step\n  \"Advance the REPL once.  Called by exactly one ticker per host; never loops on\n   `:dao.stream/blocked`.  `now` is the host's clock reading, recorded but not\n   waited on: this layer has no deadline of its own.\"\n  [state now]\n  (let [state (assoc state :last-tick now)\n        state (retry-unsent state)\n        ;; Completions and lifecycle are observed before this tick's lines are\n        ;; handled, so a `(connect …)` typed in the same tick as the drop that\n        ;; makes it legal sees the terminal fact rather than being told the\n        ;; shell is already connected.\n        state (poll-remote state now)\n        state (observe-connection state)\n        [state lines] (drain-input state)\n        state (reduce handle-line state lines)]\n    (release-queue state)))\n   - Criterion: p99 <= 250 ms, no reply lost, A delivered once, REPL step advances every round.\n   Run through bb workload-w:jolt for the independent five-minute watchdog.\n   Returns {:pass? ... :p99 ... :samples ... :elapsed-ms ... :delivered-once? ... :repl-advances? ...}.\"\n  [& {:keys [target-duration-ms target-samples]\n      :or {target-duration-ms 60000 target-samples 600}}]\n  (println \"================================================================================\")\n  (println \"J6g Workload W: Starting benchmark (target duration:\" target-duration-ms\n           \"ms, target samples:\" target-samples \")\")\n  (println \"================================================================================\")\n  (let [run-start (poller/clock-ms)\n        deadline (+ run-start 300000)\n        w (wake/make-wake)\n        server-inst (wsj/create)\n        client-b-inst (wsj/create)\n\n        ;; Peer A accounting\n        a-deliveries (atom [])\n        a-delivered-once? (atom false)\n\n        ;; Server bind\n        server-bound? (atom false)\n        server-port (atom 0)\n        _ (wsj/bind! server-inst\n                     {:bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n                      :bind-port 0\n                      :ws/max-frame-bytes 4194304\n                      :codecs [cbor/profile]\n                      :deposit! (fn [event detail]\n                                  (when (= :bind-succeeded event)\n                                    (reset! server-port (:port detail))\n                                    (reset! server-bound? true)))\n                      :accept! (fn [path seam _now]\n                                 (cond\n                                   (= path \"/peer-a\")\n                                   {:ws/adapter\n                                    {:opened! (fn [])\n                                     :binary! (fn [payload]\n                                                (swap! a-deliveries conj (alength payload)))\n                                     :message! (fn [_])\n                                     :closed! (fn [_ _])\n                                     :error! (fn [_])\n                                     :too-large! (fn [])}}\n\n                                   (= path \"/peer-b\")\n                                   (let [seam-ref (atom seam)]\n                                     {:ws/adapter\n                                      {:opened! (fn [])\n                                       :binary! (fn [payload]\n                                                  ((:send! @seam-ref) payload))\n                                       :message! (fn [msg]\n                                                   ((:send! @seam-ref) msg))\n                                       :closed! (fn [_ _])\n                                       :error! (fn [_])\n                                       :too-large! (fn [])}})))})\n\n        ;; Drive until server listener is bound\n        _ (loop []\n            (check-deadline! deadline :server-bind)\n            (when-not @server-bound?\n              (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump server-inst) nil)\n              (recur)))\n        port @server-port]\n\n    (println \"Server listening on port\" port)\n\n    ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    ;; Peer B setup: connects via client adapter\n    ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    (let [b-opened? (atom false)\n          b-samples (atom [])\n          b-outstanding (atom {})\n          b-lost (atom 0)\n          b-req-seq (atom 0)\n          b-seam (atom nil)\n          b-cb {:ws/codec cbor/profile\n                :ws/max-frame-bytes 4194304\n                :opened! #(reset! b-opened? true)\n                :binary! (fn [payload]\n                           (let [now (poller/clock-ms)\n                                 req-id (bytes->int32 payload 0)\n                                 sent-at (get @b-outstanding req-id)]\n                             (if sent-at\n                               (do (swap! b-outstanding dissoc req-id)\n                                    (swap! b-samples conj (- now sent-at))\n                                    ;; The independent sampler observes every completed reply.\n                                    (println \"W-SAMPLE\" (- now sent-at))\n                                    (flush))\n                               (swap! b-lost inc))))\n                :message! (fn [_])\n                :closed! (fn [_ _])\n                :error! (fn [_])\n                :too-large! (fn [])}]\n\n      (reset! b-seam (wsj/connect! client-b-inst\n                                   {:ws/host \"127.0.0.1\"\n                                    :ws/port port\n                                    :ws/path \"/peer-b\"}\n                                   b-cb))\n\n      ;; Drive until Peer B connection is open\n      (loop []\n        (check-deadline! deadline :peer-b-upgrade)\n        (when-not @b-opened?\n          (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump server-inst) nil)\n          (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump client-b-inst) nil)\n          (recur)))\n\n      (println \"Peer B connected and upgraded\")\n\n      ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n      ;; Peer A setup: connects via raw socket, upgrades to /peer-a\n      ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n      (let [raw-a (raw-peer! port)\n            upgrade-req (str \"GET /peer-a HTTP/1.1\\r\\n\"\n                             \"Host: 127.0.0.1:\" port \"\\r\\n\"\n                             \"Upgrade: websocket\\r\\n\"\n                             \"Connection: Upgrade\\r\\n\"\n                             \"Sec-WebSocket-Key: dGhlIHNhbXBsZSBub25jZQ==\\r\\n\"\n                             \"Sec-WebSocket-Version: 13\\r\\n\"\n                             \"Sec-WebSocket-Protocol: dao.stream.cbor\\r\\n\\r\\n\")]\n        (write-all! (:fd raw-a) (text/utf8-encode upgrade-req) deadline)\n\n        ;; Drive until Peer A upgrade response arrives\n        (loop []\n          (check-deadline! deadline :peer-a-upgrade)\n          (raw-poll! raw-a)\n          (when-not (head-end @(:in raw-a))\n            (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 (wsj/host-pump server-inst) nil)\n            (recur)))\n\n        (println \"Peer A connected and upgraded\")\n\n        ;; Prepare Peer A's 4,194,304-byte binary frame\n        (let [a-payload (bytes/alloc 4194304)\n              mask-key (byte-array [(unchecked-byte 0x37) (unchecked-byte 0xFA)\n                                    (unchecked-byte 0x21) (unchecked-byte 0x3D)])\n              a-frame (rfc6455/encode-frame {:opcode :binary\n                                             :payload a-payload\n                                             :mask-key mask-key\n                                             :fin? true})\n              total-a-frame-len (alength a-frame)\n              a-sent (atom 0)\n\n              ;; REPL loop setup\n              repl-state (atom (repl.main/boot {:adapter (host/websocket)}))\n              repl-step-count (atom 0)\n              owner-round-count (atom 0)\n\n              ;; Timing and dispatch state\n              start-time (poller/clock-ms)\n              last-10hz-tick (atom start-time)\n              last-telemetry-tick (atom start-time)\n              a-stalls (atom 0)\n              a-stalled? (atom false)\n              timed-out? (atom false)\n              max-consecutive-stalls 500\n              server-pump (wsj/host-pump server-inst)\n              client-b-pump (wsj/host-pump client-b-inst)]\n\n          (println \"Frame length for Peer A:\" total-a-frame-len \"bytes\")\n          (println \"Entering owner round loop...\")\n          (flush)\n\n          ;; Main owner loop\n          (loop []\n            (let [now (poller/clock-ms)\n                  elapsed (- now start-time)]\n\n              ;; Hard timeout guard: cap whole run at 5 minutes\n              (if (>= now deadline)\n                (do (reset! timed-out? true)\n                    (println \"HARD CAP EXCEEDED: workload-w exceeded 5 minutes (\"\n                             (- now run-start) \"ms), terminating loop.\"))\n\n                (do\n                  ;; 1. Advance owner round and step REPL loop\n                  (swap! owner-round-count inc)\n                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n                    (println \"W-PHASE repl-step\")\n                    (flush))\n                  (driver/submit-line! (:input @repl-state)\n                                       \"(loop [i 0] (if (< i 5) (recur (inc i)) i))\")\n                  (let [stepped (driver/repl-step @repl-state now)\n                        [_entries next-st] (driver/take-outbox stepped)]\n                    (reset! repl-state next-st)\n                    (swap! repl-step-count inc))\n\n                  ;; 2. Paced Peer A transfer across target-duration-ms (with no-progress guard)\n                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n                    (println \"W-PHASE peer-a-send\")\n                    (flush))\n                  (when-not @a-stalled?\n                    (let [target-bytes (if (>= elapsed target-duration-ms)\n                                         total-a-frame-len\n                                         (min total-a-frame-len\n                                              (long (* total-a-frame-len\n                                                       (/ (double elapsed) (double target-duration-ms))))))]\n                      (when (< @a-sent target-bytes)\n                        (let [to-write (min (- target-bytes @a-sent) 65536)\n                              r (write-some! (:fd raw-a) a-frame @a-sent to-write)]\n                          (cond\n                            (or (= :would-block r) (= 0 r))\n                            (let [stalls (swap! a-stalls inc)]\n                              (native/poll-one (:fd raw-a) native/pollout 0)\n                              (when (>= stalls max-consecutive-stalls)\n                                (reset! a-stalled? true)\n                                (println \"TRANSFER STALLED: Peer A hit\" stalls\n                                         \"consecutive no-progress polls at\" @a-sent \"/\" total-a-frame-len \"bytes. Aborting transfer leg.\")\n                                (flush)))\n\n                            (and (number? r) (pos? r))\n                            (do (reset! a-stalls 0)\n                                (swap! a-sent + r))\n\n                            :else\n                            (do (reset! a-stalled? true)\n                                (println \"TRANSFER STALLED: unexpected Peer A send result\" r)\n                                (flush)))))))\n\n                  ;; 3. Peer B 10 Hz dispatch: concurrent requests up to 8 outstanding\n                  (when (>= (- now @last-10hz-tick) 100)\n                    (reset! last-10hz-tick now)\n                    (when (< (count @b-outstanding) 8)\n                      (let [id (swap! b-req-seq inc)\n                            req-bs (make-1kib-request id)]\n                        (swap! b-outstanding assoc id now)\n                        ((:send! @b-seam) req-bs))))\n\n                  ;; 4. Periodic sampler flush every 10 seconds to ensure telemetry\n                  (when (>= (- now @last-telemetry-tick) 10000)\n                    (reset! last-telemetry-tick now)\n                    (let [sc (count @b-samples)\n                          cur-p99 (when (pos? sc)\n                                    (nth (sort @b-samples) (min (dec sc) (int (* 0.99 sc)))))]\n                      (println (str \"TELEMETRY: elapsed=\" (long (/ elapsed 1000)) \"s, samples=\" sc\n                                    \", running p99=\" (if cur-p99 (str cur-p99 \"ms\") \"ABSENT\") \", A-sent=\" @a-sent \"/\" total-a-frame-len\n                                    \" (\" (long (* 100 (/ (double @a-sent) (double total-a-frame-len)))) \"%), A-deliveries=\" (count @a-deliveries)\n                                    (when @a-stalled? \" [A-STALLED]\")))\n                      (flush)))\n\n                  ;; 5. Pump I/O for server and client B\n                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n                    (println \"W-PHASE server-pump\")\n                    (flush))\n                  (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 server-pump nil)\n                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n                    (println \"W-PHASE client-b-pump\")\n                    (flush))\n                  (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 client-b-pump nil)\n                  (when (= 1 @owner-round-count)\n                    (println \"W-PHASE owner-round-complete\")\n                    (flush))\n\n                  ;; Check exit conditions\n                  (let [a-done? (or @a-stalled?\n                                    (and (>= @a-sent total-a-frame-len)\n                                         (seq @a-deliveries)))\n                        time-done? (>= elapsed target-duration-ms)\n                        samples-done? (>= (count @b-samples) target-samples)]\n\n                    (if (and a-done? time-done? samples-done?)\n                      ;; Drain trailing in-flight requests briefly\n                      (let [drain-deadline (+ (poller/clock-ms) 500)]\n                        (loop []\n                          (when (and (seq @b-outstanding)\n                                     (< (poller/clock-ms) (min deadline drain-deadline)))\n                            (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 server-pump nil)\n                            (wake/sleep-fds! w 5 client-b-pump nil)\n                            (recur))))\n                      (recur)))))))\n\n          ;; Cleanup sockets\n          (raw-close! raw-a)\n          (wsj/close-host! client-b-inst)\n          (wsj/close-host! server-inst)\n          (wake/close! w)\n\n          ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------\n          ;; Evaluation of pre-registered criterion\n          ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------\n          (let [sample-count (count @b-samples)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'step-count|:steps|index-publication|defn.*summary|:budget|step-budget|:running|repl-step' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/{frontends,shell,driver}.cljc; sed -n '77,110p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '166,182p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; rg -n 'sleep-fds\"'!|poll.*ready|ready'\"' src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver*; sed -n '261,300p' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/tcp.jolt; sed -n '98,110p' bb.edn; cat .cljstyle; rg -n 'defn.*(encode-frame|parser|parse-frame)|:events' src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/rfc6455.cljc; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(defn|write-array|read-array' src/jolt/jolt/ffi*\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'step-count|:steps|index-publication|defn.*summary|:budget|step-budget|:running|repl-step' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/{frontends,shell,driver}.cljc; sed -n '77,110p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '166,182p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; rg -n 'sleep-fds\"'!|poll.*ready|ready'\"' src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver*; sed -n '261,300p' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/tcp.jolt; sed -n '98,110p' bb.edn; cat .cljstyle; rg -n 'defn.*(encode-frame|parser|parse-frame)|:events' src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/rfc6455.cljc; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(defn|write-array|read-array' src/jolt/jolt/ffi*\"","aggregated_output":"rg: src/cljc/yin/repl/shell.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc:6:   poll, print, prompt, or touch the state held here.  `repl-step` is called\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc:95:      :running? true})))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc:177:        (assoc :running? (boolean (:running? repl)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc:430:      (not (:running? state)) state\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc:579:(defn repl-step\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:992:        :running? true}))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1368:                                       :budget (min query-serve-budget\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1929:      quit [(assoc state :running? false) \"Bye\"]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2193:   :running? (:running? state)\n(defn create-state\n  ([] (create-state {}))\n  ([{:keys [input input-cursor repl host]}]\n   (let [input (or input (create-input-medium!))]\n     {:repl (or repl (repl.frontends/create-state))\n      :input input\n      :input-cursor (or input-cursor (mint-cursor input))\n      :input-ledger :untried\n      ;; The host WebSocket adapter is composition data, injected once.  Nil is\n      ;; the honest answer in a build with no host socket package.\n      :host (or host (host/websocket))\n      :connection nil\n      :adapter nil\n      :queued []\n      :outstanding nil\n      :retrying nil\n      :outbox []\n      :last-tick nil\n      :running? true})))\n\n\n(defn submit-line!\n  \"Append one typed line to the input medium and return the append outcome.\n   This is the whole of a line producer's work.\"\n  [input line]\n  (stream/append! input {line-key line}))\n\n\n(defn take-outbox\n  \"Return `[entries next-state]`, clearing the publication outbox exactly once.\"\n  [state]\n  [(:outbox state) (assoc state :outbox [])])\n\n\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Local and remote input\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- evaluate-locally\n  [state line]\n  (let [[repl text] (repl/eval-input (:repl state) line)]\n    (-> state\n        (assoc :repl repl)\n        (assoc :running? (boolean (:running? repl)))\n        (publish :yin.repl.driver/result text))))\n\n\n(defn- rpc-client\n  [state]\n9:   one read(2) per round and only after poll reported fd 0 ready, so the\n60:            (poller/eagain? e) nil ; a full pipe already owes a wake\n81:  (poller/wait-ready (:read wake) :read (poller/deadline-ms sleep-ms))\n145:  \"One read(2) of fd 0, which poll reported ready. Answers true when it\n163:(defn sleep-fds!\n166:   given) until one is ready or the earlier of `sleep-ms` and the pump's\n171:   (nil at end of input). A deadline already due still polls once, with a\n196:      (let [ready (vec (keep (fn [i]\n201:            progressed? (when pump (:progressed? ((:pump! pump) ready)))\n212:  (sleep-fds! wake sleep-ms nil line!))\n(defn recv-chunk!\n  \"One recv of at most `cap` bytes into native `buf`: `{:n n}` (n > 0),\n   `:eof`, `:would-block`, or a failure map (`:error :recv-failed`, `:class`\n   :reset for ECONNRESET). EINTR is retried.\"\n  [fd buf cap]\n  (loop []\n    (let [[n e] (recv-once fd buf cap)]\n      (cond\n        (pos? n) {:n n}\n        (zero? n) :eof\n        (native/eintr? e) (recur)\n        (native/eagain? e) :would-block\n        :else (failure :recv-failed e)))))\n\n\n(defn send-chunk!\n  \"One send of `n` bytes from native `buf`: `{:n accepted}` (possibly short,\n   possibly 0), `:would-block`, or a failure map (`:error :send-failed`,\n   `:class` :broken-pipe or :reset for a peer that has gone). EINTR is\n   retried.\"\n  [fd buf n]\n  (loop []\n    (let [[r e] (send-once fd buf n)]\n      (cond\n        (not (neg? r)) {:n r}\n        (native/eintr? e) (recur)\n        (native/eagain? e) :would-block\n        :else (failure :send-failed e)))))\n                                                \"jolt\" s))])\n                             sections)]\n           (println \"probe:jolt-ws exits\" (pr-str results))\n           (System/exit (if (every? (comp zero? second) results) 0 1)))}\n\n  workload-w:jolt\n   {:doc \"J6g: pre-registered Workload W, with an independent five-minute watchdog and ten-second sampler; one jolt worker serves two peers while stepping the REPL (needs bb bootstrap:jolt and bb build:jolt-native)\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"sh\" \"-c\"\n                          \"exec bb src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj \\\"$@\\\"\"\n                         \"jolt\" *command-line-args*)))}\n\n  build:jolt-native\n;; :namespaces is disabled project-wide. It rewrites ns forms, which is\n;; unsafe on this multi-platform codebase in two distinct ways:\n;; 1. ClojureDart uses string-prefixed :import forms (e.g.\n;;    (:import [\"dart:core\" BigInt DateTime])); the rule rewrites these\n;;    into JVM-style forms, which the cljd compiler then fails to resolve.\n;; 2. .cljc files that guard a JVM-only :import/:require clause with\n;;    #?(:cljd nil :clj ...) rely on :cljd appearing FIRST (the cljd\n;;    host-eval pass also matches :clj, so first-match-wins order is\n;;    load-bearing — see the reader-conditional trap in project memory).\n;;    The rule reorders reader-conditional branches alphabetically\n;;    (:clj before :cljd), silently re-breaking the guard on every\n;;    `cljstyle fix` — this bit dao.jing.dht.node.cljc and cost a lost\n;;    commit before being traced back here.\n{:files {:extensions #{\"blog\" \"chp\" \"clj\" \"cljc\" \"cljd\" \"cljs\" \"edn\" \"jolt\"},\n         :ignore #{\".cpcache\" \".git\" \".shadow-cljs\" \"node_modules\" \"target\"}},\n :rules {:blank-lines {:enabled? true, :max-consecutive 2},\n         :eof-newline {:enabled? true},\n         :indentation {:enabled? true},\n         :namespaces {:enabled? false},\n         :whitespace\n           {:enabled? true, :insert-missing? true, :remove-trailing? true}}}\n134:(defn encode-frame\n186:(defn parser\n358:(defn parse-frame\nzsh:1: no matches found: src/jolt/jolt/ffi*\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1900,1965p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '2160,2240p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; cat src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc; sed -n '1050,1105p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; rg -n 'step-count|:steps|step-budget|step-limit|:fuel|:tick' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '160,212p' src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt; sed -n '358,400p' src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/rfc6455.cljc; rg -n 'defn send\"'!|accepted|:outcome'\"' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/pump.jolt; rg -n 'ffi/write-array|Thread\\\\.' src/dev/jolt* | head -35; sed -n '409,432p' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1900,1965p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '2160,2240p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; cat src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc; sed -n '1050,1105p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; rg -n 'step-count|:steps|step-budget|step-limit|:fuel|:tick' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '160,212p' src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt; sed -n '358,400p' src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/rfc6455.cljc; rg -n 'defn send\"'!|accepted|:outcome'\"' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/pump.jolt; rg -n 'ffi/write-array|Thread\\\\.' src/dev/jolt* | head -35; sed -n '409,432p' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt\"","aggregated_output":"              (str \"Switched to \" (get vm-labels vm-type)\n                   (if (store/durable? (:index-store state))\n                     \" (VM store cleared; durable code index kept)\"\n                     \" (store cleared)\"))]\n             [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL VM type \" (pr-str vm-type)\n                         \"; supported: \"\n                         (pr-str (vec (keys vm-constructors))))]))\n      lang (let [lang (first args)]\n             (if (usable-binding (select-frontend (:frontends state) lang))\n               [(switch-lang state lang)\n                (str \"Switched to \" lang)]\n               [state (str \"Error: unavailable-parser: Yin REPL language \"\n                           (pr-str lang) \" is not in the frontend catalog; \"\n                           (installed-text (:frontends state)))]))\n      compile [state (render-compile-output\n                       state\n                       (compile-command-ast state (first args)))]\n      trust (trust-command state command args)\n      untrust (trust-command state command args)\n      trusted [state (str \"Own: \" (pr-str (first (:own (:link-source state))))\n                          \"\\nTrusted: \"\n                          (pr-str (vec (sort (:trusted (:admission state))))))]\n      reset [(rebuild-session\n               (configure-admission state (:initial-admission state))\n               (:vm-type state))\n             (str (get vm-labels (:vm-type state)) \" reset\")]\n      abandon (abandon-pending state)\n      help [state help-text]\n      repl-state [state (format-value (repl-state state))]\n      quit [(assoc state :running? false) \"Bye\"]\n      telemetry [state telemetry-text]\n      host [state host-text]\n      [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL command \" (pr-str command))])))\n\n\n(defn- eval-compiled\n  \"Evaluate a program `compile-input` or `compile-source` lowered.  What\n   its lowering left (`::frontend`: the session and the `:render` hook) is\n   staged on the round and committed only where the round's VM state\n   survives: when the program halts, now or when its parked require\n   completes (`finalize-eval`).  A round that fails, rolls back, or is\n   abandoned keeps the shell's previous `:frontend-session`.\"\n  [state ast]\n  (let [staged (::frontend (meta ast))\n        [state' text] (eval-program (cond-> state\n                                      staged (assoc ::frontend staged))\n                                    ast)]\n    [(dissoc state' ::frontend) text]))\n\n\n(defn- eval-parsed*\n  \"The parse dispatch of one line, against a shell with no require to\n   re-check.\"\n  [state trimmed parsed]\n  (try\n    (let [forms (:forms parsed)\n          form (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))]\n      (cond\n        (and form (command-form? form)) (handle-command state form)\n        (and form (datom-stream? form)) (eval-program state (vec form))\n        (and form (ast-map? form)) (eval-program state form)\n        forms (eval-compiled state (compile-input state trimmed forms))\n        (forms-input? state) [state (format-error (:error parsed))]\n        :else (eval-compiled state (compile-source state trimmed))))\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n      (let [[state' output-text] (drain-output state)]\n\n\n(defn repl-state\n  \"A serializable summary of shell state.\n\n   The stream summaries read the ledger rather than asking a handle whether it\n   is closed: dao.stream has no `closed?`, and an idle medium has no last\n   operation.\n   The program media are the composition's own, observed beside the VM, so\n   the shell reports what it knows of them — the declared capacity, the gaps\n   the session's observers counted, and whether a loss has already refused\n   further evaluation.  Each `:pending` entry carries the link policy's\n   name (`:manual` or `:fn`) and the pending run's `:checks`, so a host\n   can display why a run is still waiting (yin.repl.link-policy.md\n   section 3.5).  `:macros` maps each macro the expander's store holds\n   to its lambda's root address (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1).  `:index` is the\n   code indexer's `yin.repl.index/status`: whether every committed program\n   is published, whether a gap lost the indexer, and its last failure.\n   `:ast-index` is the AST indexer's `yin.repl.ast-index/status`: the sizes\n   of its `$ast` and `$occ` relations, whether a gap lost it, and why it\n   failed.\"\n  [state]\n  {:lang (:lang state)\n   :macros (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (str %1) (str %2)))\n                 (map (fn [[sym entry]]\n                        [sym (first (:yin.macro/tree entry))]))\n                 (get-in state [:expander :ctx :store]))\n   :vm {:type (:vm-type state)\n        :halted? (vm/halted? (:vm state))\n        :blocked? (vm/blocked? (:vm state))\n        :in-stream {:capacity ingress-capacity\n                    :gaps (ingress-gaps state)\n                    :lost? (boolean (:ingress-loss? state))}}\n   :running? (:running? state)\n   :output {:cursor (:output-cursor state)\n            :last-outcome (get-in state [:ledger :output] :untried)}\n   :pending (when-let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n              (let [policy (:link-policy state)]\n                (mapv (fn [p]\n                        {:name (:name p)\n                         :link-id (:yin.link/id p)\n                         :policy (if (fn? policy) :fn policy)\n                         :checks (or (:checks parked) 0)})\n                      (:links parked))))\n   :index (index/status (:indexer state))\n   :ast-index (ast-index/status (:ast-indexer state))\n   :telemetry {:supported? false :note telemetry-text}\n   :remote {:connected? false}})\n(ns yin.repl.frontends\n  \"The REPL's standard frontend catalog (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section\n   8.5.6, slice F2): the hand-written Clojure and PHP frontends and the\n   ANTLR Python frontend installed into a `yang.frontend` catalog. This is\n   the only place the REPL composition names a language's namespace;\n   `yin.repl` core steps whatever binding the catalog selects.\n\n   A binding is `{:parse (fn [input]) :lower (fn [parsed])}`, with\n   `:input :forms` when the frontend consumes the forms the shell reader\n   already read, else the source text.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\n    [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n    [yang.php :as yang.php]\n    #?@(:cljd [[yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.antlr.repl]\n               [yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\n               [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.antlr.probe]]\n        :default [[yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.antlr.repl]\n                  [yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\n                  [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.antlr.probe]])\n    [yin.repl :as repl]))\n\n\n(defn- manifest\n  [id language]\n  {:yang.frontend/id id,\n   :yang.frontend/spi 1,\n   :yang.frontend/revision \"legacy-1\",\n   :yang.frontend/language language,\n   :yang.frontend/grammar {:yang.grammar/package \"none\",\n                           :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"program\"},\n                           :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1},\n   :yang.frontend/options-schema :segment/none,\n   :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :segment/legacy,\n   :yang.frontend/runtime-profile :segment/legacy,\n   :yang.frontend/support-profile :segment/legacy})\n\n\n(defn- clojure-lower\n  [forms]\n  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n\n\n(defn- antlr-manifest\n  []\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/python :python)\n         :yang.frontend/revision \"f4\"\n         :yang.frontend/grammar\n         {:yang.grammar/package \"python3\",\n          :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"file_input\"},\n          :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1,\n          :yang.grammar/targets #{:java :javascript :dart}}))\n\n\n(defn standard\n  \"The standard catalog. The Clojure frontend consumes the forms the\n   shell's own reader read, so its parse stage is the identity.  The ANTLR\n   frontend is the Python frontend, installed on every host, each running\n   its own generated target of the one grammar.  It shows what a submission\n   printed and the value rendered by its `:render` (Python repr).\"\n  []\n  (cond-> frontend/empty-catalog\n    true (frontend/install (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n                           {:input :forms,\n                            :parse identity,\n                            :lower clojure-lower})\n    true (frontend/install (manifest :yang/php :php)\n                           {:parse identity, :lower yang.php/compile})\n    #?@(:cljd [true (frontend/install\n                      (antlr-manifest)\n                      {:parse (fn [source]\n                                (python.antlr.parser/parse-source (str source \"\\n\"))),\n                       :lower python.antlr.repl/lower,\n                       :primitives python.antlr.repl/primitives,\n                       :lower-session python.antlr.repl/lower-session,\n                       :render python.antlr.repl/display-value,\n                       :probe python.antlr.probe/probe})]\n        ;; jolt (J5): installed over the C++ parser when native/jolt-parser\n        ;; is available; otherwise left out, so (lang :yang/python) answers\n        ;; unavailable-parser, never another parser\n        :jolt [(python.antlr.parser/available?)\n               (frontend/install\n                 (antlr-manifest)\n                 {;; a :parser-budget or :unavailable-parser refusal names\n                  ;; the language it refused\n                  :parse (fn [source]\n                           (try (python.antlr.parser/parse-source (str source \"\\n\"))\n                                (catch Exception e\n                                  (if (#{:parser-budget :unavailable-parser}\n                                       (:diagnostic (ex-data e)))\n                                    (throw (ex-info (ex-message e)\n                                                    (assoc (ex-data e) :lang :yang/python)\n                                                    e))\n                                    (throw e))))),\n                  :lower python.antlr.repl/lower,\n                  :primitives python.antlr.repl/primitives,\n                  :lower-session python.antlr.repl/lower-session,\n                  :render python.antlr.repl/display-value,\n                  :probe python.antlr.probe/probe})]\n        :default [true (frontend/install\n                         (antlr-manifest)\n                         {:parse (fn [source]\n                                   (python.antlr.parser/parse-source (str source \"\\n\"))),\n                          :lower python.antlr.repl/lower,\n                          :primitives python.antlr.repl/primitives,\n                          :lower-session python.antlr.repl/lower-session,\n                          :render python.antlr.repl/display-value,\n                          :probe python.antlr.probe/probe})])))\n\n\n(defn create-state\n  \"`yin.repl/create-state` composed with the standard catalog unless the\n   host supplies its own `:frontends`.  Each binding registers its own\n   `:primitives`; none is merged ambiently.\"\n  ([] (create-state {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (repl/create-state (update opts :frontends #(or % (standard))))))\n(defn step-all\n  \"One tick of the single step owner: the local shell first, then the served\n   endpoint, against the same shell value.  A DHT index store's node is stepped\n   first (yin.repl.dht/step): its lines print before the shell's, a\n   hydration still outstanding leaves every typed line waiting in the\n   input medium, and a refused one stops the shell.  The custody control\n   plane is stepped next, before the refusal and admission branches, so\n   renewals, pending releases and request retries continue during\n   hydration and past a refusal.  A `--port` process\n   serves one shared shell, as v1's atom made it: the driver evaluates this\n   tick's local\n   lines first, so a definition typed at the local prompt is already in the\n   shell the endpoint evaluates remote requests against in the same tick, and\n   the endpoint's shell (remote definitions included) is threaded back\n   before the next tick.  The custody program step follows the driver's own\n   step and precedes the endpoint's; once the shell has stopped it is\n   replaced by the stop latch, so no custody program call runs after\n   `:running?` turns false.  A require parked on a closure load the node\n   ended this tick is re-checked once, before any typed line, with no line\n   of its own (yin.repl/recheck-on-tick, yin.vm.linker.dht.md 8.2),\n   and linker progress resumes a parked run (7.5): its text prints after the\n   node's lines.  Returns `[state server lines]`;\n   the caller only prints.\"\n  [state server now]\n  (let [[repl dht-lines events] (repl.dht/step (:repl state) now)\n        state (custody-control-step (assoc state :repl repl))]\n    (cond\n      (repl.dht/refusal repl)\n      [(custody-stop (assoc state :running? false)) server dht-lines]\n\n      (not (repl.dht/admitting? repl))\n      [state server dht-lines]\n\n      :else\n      (let [[repl rechecked] (shell/recheck-on-tick (:repl state) events)\n            dht-lines (cond-> dht-lines\n                        (seq rechecked) (conj rechecked))\n            state (assoc state :repl repl)\n            stepped (driver/repl-step state now)\n            stepped (if (:running? stepped)\n                      (custody-program-step stepped)\n                      (custody-stop stepped))\n            [entries state'] (driver/take-outbox stepped)\n            server' (when server\n                      (serve/step (assoc-in server [:repl] (:repl state'))\n                                  now))\n            [server-entries server''] (if server'\n                                        (serve/take-outbox server')\n                                        [[] nil])\n            state'' (if server'' (assoc state' :repl (:repl server'')) state')]\n        [state'' server'' (into dht-lines\n                                (map entry-text)\n                                (into (vec entries) server-entries))]))))\n\n\n(defn moved?\n;; One owner round\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn sleep-fds!\n  \"One owner round's wait (plan v2 A1): poll the wake pipe, fd 0 (when\n   `line!` is given) and `pump`'s interest descriptors (when `pump` is\n   given) until one is ready or the earlier of `sleep-ms` and the pump's\n   `:deadline` (`jolt.io-poller/clock-ms`; nil, or a pump without one, is\n   the cadence alone) passes; then drain the wake pipe, run one\n   `(:pump! pump)` turn over the observed `[[fd revents] ...]` (every\n   round; `[]` after a timeout), then deposit stdin lines through `line!`\n   (nil at end of input). A deadline already due still polls once, with a\n   zero timeout, so readiness seen then reaches the same `pump!` turn as\n   the expiry. Never evaluates. Answers truthy when anything was woken,\n   moved or deposited.\"\n  [wake sleep-ms pump line!]\n  (let [interest (if pump (vec ((:interest pump))) [])\n        base (if line! 2 1)\n        n (+ base (count interest))\n        fds (native/alloc-pollfds n)\n        cadence (poller/deadline-ms sleep-ms)\n        due (when-let [f (:deadline pump)] (f))\n        deadline (if due (min due cadence) cadence)]\n    (try\n      (native/init-pollfd! fds 0 (:read wake) native/pollin)\n      (when line! (native/init-pollfd! fds 1 0 native/pollin))\n      (dotimes [i (count interest)]\n        (let [[fd events] (nth interest i)]\n          (native/init-pollfd! fds (+ base i) fd events)))\n      (loop []\n        (let [remaining (max 0 (long (Math/ceil (- deadline (poller/clock-ms)))))\n              [rc e] (native/c-poll fds n remaining)]\n          (cond\n            (and (neg? rc) (native/eintr? e)) (recur)\n            (neg? rc) (throw (ex-info \"owner poll failed\" {:errno e}))\n            :else nil)))\n      (let [ready (vec (keep (fn [i]\n                               (let [rev (native/pollfd-revents fds (+ base i))]\n                                 (when (pos? rev) [(first (nth interest i)) rev])))\n                             (range (count interest))))\n            woken? (drain! wake)\n            progressed? (when pump (:progressed? ((:pump! pump) ready)))\n            stdin? (when (and line! (pos? (native/pollfd-revents fds 1)))\n                     (read-stdin! wake line!))]\n        (or woken? progressed? stdin?))\n      (finally (ffi/free fds)))))\n\n\n(defn sleep-input!\n  \"Wait for a nudge, stdin, or the cadence deadline. `line!` only deposits\n   lines (nil at EOF). Never evaluate from this seam.\"\n  [wake sleep-ms line!]\n  (sleep-fds! wake sleep-ms nil line!))\n(defn parse-frame\n  \"Resume parsing `chunk` at `offset` until one event is produced or the\n   chunk is exhausted: `[event-or-nil parser' offset']`.  `offset'` is the\n   first byte not consumed, so a caller that stops after an event keeps the\n   rest of its chunk by offset and resumes later with the same chunk and\n   `offset'`; nothing is copied or re-read.  With a nil event `offset'` is the\n   chunk length and any partial frame is held in `parser'`.  An event is a\n   completed control frame, a completed message (non-final data frames\n   produce none), or a failure; a done parser answers `[nil parser offset]`.\n   The chunk is never mutated.\"\n  [state chunk offset]\n  (let [n (bytes/length chunk)]\n    (loop [st state i offset]\n      (cond\n        (= :done (:phase st)) [nil st i]\n        (>= i n) [nil st n]\n\n        (= :header (:phase st))\n        (let [hdr (conj (:hdr st) (bytes/get chunk i))\n              c (count hdr)\n              st (assoc st :hdr hdr)\n              early (when (= c 2) (check-first-two st (nth hdr 0) (nth hdr 1)))]\n          (cond\n            early (let [[s es] (fail st (first early) (second early))]\n                    [(first es) s (inc i)])\n            (and (>= c 2) (= c (header-length (nth hdr 1))))\n            (let [[st' es] (begin-frame st hdr)]\n              (cond\n                (seq es) [(first es) st' (inc i)]\n                (and (= :payload (:phase st')) (zero? (:len (:frame st'))))\n                (let [[s es2] (finish-frame st')]\n                  (if (seq es2)\n                    [(first es2) s (inc i)]\n                    (recur s (inc i))))\n                (= :done (:phase st'))\n                [nil st' (inc i)]\n                :else (recur st' (inc i))))\n            :else (recur st (inc i))))\n\n        :else\n        (let [{:keys [len got]} (:frame st)\n              take (min (- len got) (- n i))\n              [st' failure] (take-payload st chunk i take)]\n27:   `queued-bytes` counts every byte handed over and not yet accepted by the\n114:  \"Default per-listener cap on accepted, not yet upgraded sockets (A4).\"\n222:   without one, accepted descriptors are closed), `:on-accept-error`,\n305:  \"Bytes handed to `h` and not yet accepted by the kernel: exact, 0 after\n406:   kernel accepted (0 on EAGAIN), or a failure map.\"\n442:(defn send!\n444:   connection `h`. Answers nil (accepted: on the wire or queued) or\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_stack.clj:17:;; thread (the jolt main thread; a thread jolt starts with Thread.):\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_gc.clj:53:        _ (ffi/write-array in bs)\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_gc.clj:59:        u (Thread. (fn [] (while (not @stop) (swap! ticks conj (ms)) (Thread/sleep 5))))\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_gc.clj:60:        p (Thread. (fn []\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_cycles.clj:89:      (when (pos? n) (ffi/write-array in bs))\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_parity.clj:374:      (when (pos? n) (ffi/write-array in bs))\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_faults.clj:43:(def orig-write ffi/write-array)\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_faults.clj:123:        outcome (with-redefs-fn {#'ffi/alloc alloc, #'ffi/write-array write,\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_workers.clj:162:                  (Thread.\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_workers.clj:208:    (ffi/write-array in src)\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_workers.clj:234:      th (Thread. (fn []\nsrc/dev/jolt_smoke.clj:84:        th (Thread. (fn []\nsrc/dev/jolt_j5_measure.clj:77:      (when (pos? n) (ffi/write-array in bs))\nsrc/dev/jolt_j5_measure.clj:109:  (let [t (Thread. #(run opts))]\nsrc/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj:108:               (ffi/write-array p bs off (- n off))\nsrc/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj:137:        (ffi/write-array p bs off n)\nsrc/dev/jolt_j5_budget.clj:122:      (when (pos? n) (ffi/write-array in bs))\nsrc/dev/jolt_tcp_probe.clj:201:      (ffi/write-array p bs)\nsrc/dev/jolt_tcp_probe.clj:377:                (ffi/write-array p payload)\nsrc/dev/jolt_tcp_probe.clj:578:                     (ffi/write-array buf flood)\nsrc/dev/jolt_tcp_probe.clj:634:      (fn [p] (ffi/write-array p bs) (poller/c-write fd p (alength bs))))))\nsrc/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj:276:      (ffi/write-array p bs)\nsrc/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj:293:      (ffi/write-array p bs)\nsrc/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj:64:      (when (pos? n) (ffi/write-array in src))\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_stack_child.clj:65:      (ffi/write-array in bs)\nsrc/dev/jolt_j0c_stack_child.clj:116:    (let [t (Thread. #(run shape mode max-ms depths))]\nsrc/dev/jolt_udp_probe.clj:98:      (when (pos? len) (ffi/write-array buf payload))\n(defn- accept-upgrade!\n  \"A complete, accepted upgrade on raw connection `c`: the 101 is queued, the\n   connection turns :ws, and the composition's `accept!` gets its seam.\"\n  [inst lrec c request response rest]\n  (let [p (::pump inst)\n        h (:h @c)\n        {:keys [accept! adapter-of max-frame]} @lrec\n        subprotocol (some-> (:subprotocol response) codec/codec-name)]\n    (if (pump/send! p h (text/utf8-encode (:response response)))\n      ;; the 101 could not be written: the pump reports :on-error\n      nil\n      (do (pump/upgraded! p h (protocol :server max-frame) rest)\n          (swap! c assoc :phase :open)\n          (let [target (or (upgrade/canonical-path (:target request)) (:target request))\n                result (try (accept! target (assoc (seam p c :server) :ws/subprotocol subprotocol)\n                                     (System/currentTimeMillis))\n                            (catch Throwable _ ::threw))]\n            (if (= ::threw result)\n              (do (upgrade-failed! lrec :yin.repl.endpoint/upgrade-threw)\n                  (pump/close! p h 1011 \"dao.stream/upgrade-failed\"))\n              (swap! c assoc :cb (adapter-of result))))))))\n\n\n(defn- server-head!\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The adapter’s send seam must stay on the owner thread. I’ll have B’s dedicated thread put timestamped offers on a stream, then let the owner send them. That preserves the independent 100 ms grid and measures time spent waiting for the owner.\n\nI also found that `driver/repl-step` evaluates local submissions synchronously. I’ll submit the loop once and report driver-step counts explicitly; those counts won’t imply that the VM keeps evaluating the loop on later rounds."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,165p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '1,120p' src/cljc/dao/stream.cljc; sed -n '134,156p' src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/rfc6455.cljc; sed -n '186,208p' src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/rfc6455.cljc; sed -n '500,545p' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt; rg -n 'cljstyle' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; rg -n 'defn (head-parser|check-response|client-request)|outcome' src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/upgrade.cljc | tail -18; sed -n '1,55p' src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,165p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '1,120p' src/cljc/dao/stream.cljc; sed -n '134,156p' src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/rfc6455.cljc; sed -n '186,208p' src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/rfc6455.cljc; sed -n '500,545p' src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt; rg -n 'cljstyle' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; rg -n 'defn (head-parser|check-response|client-request)|outcome' src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/upgrade.cljc | tail -18; sed -n '1,55p' src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.repl.driver\n  \"The one owner of Yin REPL state.\n\n   A line producer appends `{:yin.repl.input/line \\\"…\\\"}` to the\n   composition-owned input medium and returns.  It does not evaluate, request,\n   poll, print, prompt, or touch the state held here.  `repl-step` is called\n   once per externally driven tick by exactly one ticker per host: it drains\n   the input medium, evaluates local input, forwards ordinary source through\n   the RPC client, publishes completions exactly once, and returns the next\n   state.\n\n   It never loops on `blocked`, and it owns no promise, future, callback, atom,\n   or clock.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.data :as data]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]\n            [yin.repl.adapter :as adapter]\n            [yin.repl.connect :as connect]\n            [yin.repl :as repl]\n            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]\n            [yin.repl.host :as host]))\n\n\n(def line-key :yin.repl.input/line)\n\n\n(def input-capacity\n  \"Declared capacity of the composition-owned input medium, in elements.\"\n  1024)\n\n\n(def input-budget\n  \"Maximum input elements one step reads, so a flooded medium cannot make a\n   single step unbounded.\"\n  64)\n\n\n(def response-budget\n  \"Maximum response-medium elements one step reads.\"\n  32)\n\n\n(def event-key :yin.repl.driver/event)\n(def text-key :yin.repl.driver/text)\n\n\n(def ^:private diagnostic-bounds\n  \"Bound on operator-facing diagnostic text built from unbounded internal\n   state (raw input, event/result maps).\"\n  {:depth 3 :items 8 :chars 200})\n\n\n(def connect-usage\n  (str \"(connect \\\"daostream:ws://host:port/repl\\\" [:codec :cbor|:transit]) \"\n       \"— an absent path means /repl, an absent codec means :cbor\"))\n\n\n(defn create-input-medium!\n  \"Create the composition-owned input ring buffer.  The handoff between a line\n   producer and the step owner is a stream, which is what makes it explicit and\n   thread-safe.\"\n  []\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n                   ring/capacity-key input-capacity})))\n\n\n(defn- mint-cursor\n  [handle]\n  (let [result (stream/cursor handle :dao.stream/oldest)]\n    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n      (:dao.stream/cursor result))))\n\n\n(defn create-state\n  ([] (create-state {}))\n  ([{:keys [input input-cursor repl host]}]\n   (let [input (or input (create-input-medium!))]\n     {:repl (or repl (repl.frontends/create-state))\n      :input input\n      :input-cursor (or input-cursor (mint-cursor input))\n      :input-ledger :untried\n      ;; The host WebSocket adapter is composition data, injected once.  Nil is\n      ;; the honest answer in a build with no host socket package.\n      :host (or host (host/websocket))\n      :connection nil\n      :adapter nil\n      :queued []\n      :outstanding nil\n      :retrying nil\n      :outbox []\n      :last-tick nil\n      :running? true})))\n\n\n(defn submit-line!\n  \"Append one typed line to the input medium and return the append outcome.\n   This is the whole of a line producer's work.\"\n  [input line]\n  (stream/append! input {line-key line}))\n\n\n(defn take-outbox\n  \"Return `[entries next-state]`, clearing the publication outbox exactly once.\"\n  [state]\n  [(:outbox state) (assoc state :outbox [])])\n\n\n(defn attach-remote\n  [state adapter-state]\n  (assoc state :adapter adapter-state :queued [] :outstanding nil :retrying nil))\n\n\n(defn detach-remote\n  [state]\n  (assoc state :adapter nil :queued [] :outstanding nil :retrying nil))\n\n\n(defn- publish\n  [state event text]\n  (if (str/blank? (str text))\n    state\n    (update state :outbox conj {event-key event text-key text})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Input\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- drain-input\n  \"Read up to `input-budget` input elements, total over every `next` outcome.\n   A gap means typed lines were evicted: the loss is published, the recovery\n   cursor is taken, and none of the missing input is evaluated.\"\n  [state]\n  (loop [remaining input-budget\n         state state\n         lines []]\n    (if (or (zero? remaining) (nil? (:input-cursor state)))\n      [state lines]\n      (let [result (stream/next (:input state) (:input-cursor state))\n            outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n        (case outcome\n          :dao.stream/ok\n          (recur (dec remaining)\n                 (assoc state :input-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result))\n                 (conj lines (get (:dao.stream/value result) line-key)))\n\n          :dao.stream/gap\n          (recur (dec remaining)\n                 (-> state\n                     (assoc :input-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result))\n                     (publish :yin.repl.driver/notice\n                              \";; input lost: typed lines were evicted before this step\"))\n                 lines)\n\n          :dao.stream/blocked\n          [(assoc state :input-ledger outcome) lines]\n\n          [(-> state\n               (assoc :input-ledger outcome)\n               (publish :yin.repl.driver/notice\n                        (str \";; input \" (name outcome))))\n           lines])))))\n(ns dao.stream\n  \"DaoStream v2: passive substrate for IO in datom.world.\n\n   Seven operations:\n     Five handle operations (protocols implemented per declared surface):\n       descriptor (universal reachability and identity projection)\n       cursor     (reader surface)\n       next       (reader surface)\n       append!    (writer surface)\n       close!     (closable surface)\n     Two transport entry functions (per-transport, host-composed):\n       create!    (creates a new logical stream from a creation specification)\n       attach!    (attaches to an existing stream via portable descriptor)\n\n   Result Convention:\n     Every operation returns an open outcome map keyed by :dao.stream/outcome.\n     All qualified keywords live under :dao.stream/…\n     Each operation has an exhaustive, closed outcome set.\"\n  (:refer-clojure :exclude [next]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The Seven Operations and Standard Keywords\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def operations\n  \"The seven DaoStream v2 operations.\"\n  #{:create! :attach! :descriptor :cursor :next :append! :close!})\n\n\n(def surfaces\n  \"The public operational surfaces a handle may declare.\"\n  #{:reader :writer :closable})\n\n\n;; Anchors\n(def anchor-oldest\n  \"Earliest retained position on the stream.\"\n  :dao.stream/oldest)\n\n\n(def anchor-newest\n  \"Positioned after the newest appended value (observes next arrival).\"\n  :dao.stream/newest)\n\n\n(def standard-anchors\n  \"Contract-defined anchor keywords.\"\n  #{anchor-oldest anchor-newest})\n\n\n;; Closed outcome sets per operation (contract exhaustive tables)\n(def outcomes-create\n  #{:dao.stream/ok\n    :dao.stream/invalid-spec\n    :dao.stream/not-found\n    :dao.stream/transport-error})\n\n\n(def outcomes-attach\n  #{:dao.stream/ok\n    :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor\n    :dao.stream/not-found\n    :dao.stream/transport-error})\n\n\n(def outcomes-descriptor\n  #{:dao.stream/ok})\n\n\n(def outcomes-cursor\n  #{:dao.stream/ok\n    :dao.stream/invalid-anchor\n    :dao.stream/closed\n    :dao.stream/refused\n    :dao.stream/transport-error})\n\n\n(def outcomes-next\n  #{:dao.stream/ok\n    :dao.stream/blocked\n    :dao.stream/end\n    :dao.stream/gap\n    :dao.stream/cursor-mismatch\n    :dao.stream/invalid-cursor\n    :dao.stream/refused\n    :dao.stream/transport-error})\n\n\n(def outcomes-append\n  #{:dao.stream/ok\n    :dao.stream/full\n    :dao.stream/invalid-value\n    :dao.stream/closed\n    :dao.stream/refused\n    :dao.stream/transport-error})\n\n\n(def outcomes-close\n  #{:dao.stream/ok})\n\n\n(def operation-outcomes\n  \"Map of operation keyword to its closed outcome set.\"\n  {:create! outcomes-create\n   :attach! outcomes-attach\n   :descriptor outcomes-descriptor\n   :cursor outcomes-cursor\n   :next outcomes-next\n   :append! outcomes-append\n   :close! outcomes-close})\n\n\n(def outcome-required-keys\n  \"Map from [operation outcome] to required keys in the result map.\"\n  {[:create! :dao.stream/ok] #{:dao.stream/handle}\n   [:attach! :dao.stream/ok] #{:dao.stream/handle}\n   [:descriptor :dao.stream/ok] #{:dao.stream/descriptor :dao.stream/identity}\n   [:cursor :dao.stream/ok] #{:dao.stream/cursor}\n   [:next :dao.stream/ok] #{:dao.stream/value :dao.stream/cursor}\n(defn encode-frame\n  \"The wire bytes of one frame: `{:opcode :payload}` plus optional `:fin?`\n   (default true) and `:mask-key` (four bytes; present for client frames).\n   Header and masked payload are written into one fresh array; `:payload`\n   is left unchanged.  A control frame over 125 bytes or not final throws.\"\n  [{:keys [opcode payload mask-key fin?] :or {fin? true}}]\n  (let [op (opcode-int opcode)\n        n (bytes/length payload)]\n    (when (and (>= op 8) (or (> n 125) (not fin?)))\n      (throw (ex-info \"control frames are final and at most 125 bytes\"\n                      {:opcode op :length n})))\n    (let [lenb (length-bytes n)\n          mask? (some? mask-key)\n          head (into [(bit-or (if fin? 0x80 0) op)\n                      (bit-or (if mask? 0x80 0) (first lenb))]\n                     (concat (rest lenb) (when mask? (bytes/to-vector mask-key))))\n          hn (count head)\n          out (bytes/alloc (+ hn n))]\n      (loop [i 0]\n        (when (< i hn)\n          (bytes/set! out i (nth head i))\n          (recur (inc i))))\n      (if mask?\n(defn parser\n  \"A fresh parser.  `:role` is `:server` or `:client` (whose frames it\n   parses are the peer's); `:max-message-bytes` bounds an assembled message\n   (default `absolute-ceiling`).\"\n  [{:keys [role max-message-bytes]}]\n  {:role role\n   :max (min absolute-ceiling (or max-message-bytes absolute-ceiling))\n   :phase :header\n   :hdr []\n   :frame nil\n   :msg nil})\n\n\n(defn- fail\n  [state code reason]\n  [(assoc state :phase :done)\n   [{:type :fail :code code :reason reason}]])\n\n\n(defn- header-length\n  \"Total header bytes the first two bytes `b0 b1` promise.\"\n  [b1]\n  (+ 2\n  \"Bind a listener (R1). `opts`: `:bind-host` (a literal or localhost),\n   `:bind-port` (0 asks the kernel), `:accept!` `(fn [path seam now])`,\n   `:deposit!`, `:codecs` (the endpoint's codec table; nil accepts any or\n   no subprotocol), `:ws/max-frame-bytes`, `:ws.jolt/adapter-of` (the\n   callback map for an `accept!` result; default its `:ws/adapter`),\n   `:ws.jolt/max-connections`, `:ws.jolt/upgrade-timeout-ms`,\n   `:ws.jolt/close-deadline-ms`. Deposits `:bind-succeeded` with the actual\n   port before answering `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   :ws.jolt/listener lh :ws.jolt/instance inst}`; a bind or listen failure\n   answers a transport error and deposits nothing.\"\n  [inst {:keys [bind-host bind-port deposit!] :as opts}]\n  (let [addr (tcp/parse-address bind-host bind-port)\n        l (when-not (:error addr) (tcp/listen! addr))]\n    (if (or (not (live? inst)) (:error addr) (not (:fd l)))\n      transport-error\n      (let [p (::pump inst)\n            lrec (atom {:opts opts\n                        :accept! (:accept! opts)\n                        :adapter-of (or (:ws.jolt/adapter-of opts) :ws/adapter)\n                        :max-frame (:ws/max-frame-bytes opts)\n                        :close-deadline-ms (:ws.jolt/close-deadline-ms opts)\n                        :unbind-deposit! nil})\n            lh (pump/listener!\n                 p (:fd l)\n                 {:on-accept (gated inst #(accepted! inst lrec %))\n                  :on-accept-error (gated inst (fn [_]\n                                                 (deposit! :listener-error\n                                                           {:code :yin.repl.endpoint/listener-error\n                                                            :message \"the host listener reported an error\"})))\n                  :on-drained (gated inst #(when-let [d (:unbind-deposit! @lrec)]\n                                             (d :stopped {:code :yin.repl.endpoint/stopped\n                                                          :message \"the host listener stopped\"})))\n                  :max-pending-upgrades pump/max-pending-upgrades\n                  :upgrade-timeout-ms (or (:ws.jolt/upgrade-timeout-ms opts)\n                                          (:upgrade-timeout-ms (::opts inst))\n                                          pump/upgrade-timeout-ms)\n                  :max-connections (:ws.jolt/max-connections opts)})]\n        (swap! lrec assoc :lh lh)\n        (swap! (st inst) assoc-in [:listeners (:id lh)] lrec)\n        (deposit! :bind-succeeded {:host bind-host, :port (:port l)})\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n         :ws.jolt/listener lh\n         :ws.jolt/instance inst}))))\n\n\n(defn- owned-by\n95:change (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\n487:| `shiva.stigmergy.systems` | 24 / 62 GB | Server snapshot: java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.1. The repo's `mise.toml` selects Flutter `latest` on beta, not a fixed version. Activate the repo toolchain before running any lane. |\n488:| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | Server snapshot (rechecked 2026-10-29): java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.8 (the stale hand-symlinked 3.41.9 was replaced via `mise install flutter@3.47.8` after it failed to compile `dart:ui`-using cljd namespaces; if the Dart lane dies in the cljd compile, check `mise ls flutter` first). Tri-host quick tier verified green on 2026-10-29 (see Measured times). |\n39:(defn head-parser\n261:  {:outcome :refuse :status status :reason reason\n269:   `{:outcome :accept :response head-text :subprotocol codec-or-nil}` or\n270:   `{:outcome :refuse :status :reason :response head-text}`.  Extensions the\n293:          {:outcome :accept\n325:(defn client-request\n358:(defn check-response\n361:   `{:outcome :ok :subprotocol name-or-nil}` or\n362:   `{:outcome :failed :reason kw}`.  Any `Sec-WebSocket-Extensions` header\n368:      (:error response) {:outcome :failed :reason :malformed}\n369:      (= 426 (:status response)) {:outcome :failed :reason :version-rejected}\n370:      (not= 101 (:status response)) {:outcome :failed :reason :status}\n371:      (not (has-token? headers \"upgrade\" \"websocket\")) {:outcome :failed :reason :upgrade}\n372:      (not (has-token? headers \"connection\" \"upgrade\")) {:outcome :failed :reason :connection}\n375:      {:outcome :failed :reason :accept}\n377:      {:outcome :failed :reason :unsolicited-extension}\n379:      {:outcome :failed :reason :unsolicited-subprotocol}\n380:      :else {:outcome :ok :subprotocol protocol})))\n;; bb probe:jolt-ws: the J6e gates for the jolt WebSocket host adapter\n;; (dao.stream.ws.jolt over the J6d pump and substrate, with the J6b frame and\n;; upgrade cores and J6c's SHA-1), one section per child jolt process so an\n;; abort cannot erase another section's report:\n;;\n;;   closure    C1: the adapter, pump, substrate, cores and crypto are loaded\n;;              with jolt.socket.native, jolt.io-poller and jolt.ffi; neither\n;;              jolt.socket (the java.net shim) nor dao.stream.transit is;\n;;   handshake  C2: jolt dials jolt (CBOR negotiated, the seam names it); the\n;;              RFC 6455 sample key's accept value through libcrypto SHA-1;\n;;              server refusals (Transit-only offer, no subprotocol, not an\n;;              upgrade, a 9 KiB head, a stalled head at the overridden\n;;              deadline), each with its one :upgrade-failed; client failures\n;;              (426, bad accept key, unsolicited extension, oversized 101,\n;;              refused connect), each exactly one :closed! 1006\n;;              connect-failed; wss:// dials nothing;\n;;   bind       C3: port 0 deposits :bind-succeeded with the kernel's port\n;;              inside bind!; serve! reaches :serving naming it; a port in use\n;;              is a transport error (::bind-failed); 0.0.0.0 by literal;\n;;   address    C4: literals, [::1] and localhost dial; a host name is a\n;;              transport error at attach! with the REPL's reachability text;\n;;              the resolver trap is never sprung;\n;;   io         C5: the transport over the real adapter: exact :queued-bytes\n;;              behind a scripted short write, outbound high water (full, then\n;;              ok after drain), outbound overflow (1008, closed), a message\n;;              over the frame bound (frame-too-large, 1009, never delivered),\n;;              EOF and reset (one :ws/closed 1006), send after failure, a\n;;              150 KB message both ways;\n;;   close      C6: close-ended! 4000 (:ws/ended both sides), 1000\n;;              (:ws/closed), the empty close (1005, empty response), 5000\n;;              (1002 both ways), a non-reading peer (1006 at the overridden\n;;              deadline);\n;;   shutdown   C7: (quit) through the real owner loop (main/run-owner!) with\n;;              two acknowledged jolt REPL peers on a second instance, a\n;;              non-reading peer holding pending bytes and a continuously\n;;              readable peer: :stopped before the unconfirmed verdict, 4000 at\n;;              both peers, the non-reading peer shut within the unbind grace,\n;;              the registry empty before close-host!, drained/forced per\n;;              connection, :unbind-closed 0, fewer rounds than stop-ticks\n;;              and no timeout text; the same gate with a peer readable at\n;;              every poll (R17), which receives 4000 from the composition;\n;;              the 1001 slot exists only when no upgraded connection remains;\n;;              then a\n;;              one-tick budget: forced, and close-host! leaves nothing;\n;;   isolation  C8: two instances, each a listener and a dial, interleaved;\n;;              no cross-talk; close-host! on one leaves the other serving;\n;;   driver     C9: driver/sleep-fds! folds the deadline: an empty registry\n;;              waits the cadence, a 50 ms deadline under a 1000 ms cadence\n;;              wakes at about 50 ms, a past deadline still polls and hands a\n;;              ready fd and the expiry to one pump!; a --headless --port\n;;              child process answers a connected peer (R11);\n;;   fairness   C10: a readable connection plus runnable REPL work: the step\n;;              and the delivered-frame counts both advance every round.\n;;\n;; The adapter sections run under the native-memory ledger of the J6d probe\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
